CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ dereference of a reference to a pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A cast to a reference type is the address of its operand typed as the
reference; `*' was applied to that address, so `*static_cast<int *&>(p)'
was p itself rather than the int it points to.
